     <period-end iso-date="2025-04-15"></period-end>
     <target value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mostly achieved. The parametric pilot schemes have progressed on three fronts: (a) an insurance scheme for Cocoa producers in two municipalities of the Santander department, with insurance policies issued by a private company for around US$3 million in 2024 and US$3.6 million in 2025, benefiting around 2,400 producers and covering around 3,000 ha in 2024 and 3,500 ha in 2025; (b) the MCC (&#x201c;Modelo de Compensaci&#xf3;n Campesina&#x201d;) established with the coffee producers association, whose policy was issued in December 2025 by a public insurance company; and (c) a parametric insurance scheme for 14 municipalities in the departments of Choc&#xf3;, C&#xf3;rdoba, Sucre, Meta, and Cundinamarca oriented towards small farmers and sponsored by MADR, whose policy is expected to be issued in June 2026.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="2"></actual>
